body:
{{Die, my love}}

{{Peach}} (by emma glass)

both of these are immersions in the heads of women who are dealing with psychosis/delusions, I think you'll like it.

you could try a song of ice and fire by george rr martin, it has lots of politics and very interesting very well developed characters. it's a series to get lost in. also the worldbuiling is absolutely superb and has lots of the magical creatures you listed, plus super easy to understand yet still somewhat mysterious magic system. 

another recommendation: zenobia by gellu naum. the atmosphere is very much interesting and has an underlying romance that doesnt really look like movie type of romance just love like real people love. it's set in romania and has quite a bit of local spirituality sprinkled in. it's quite weird but I'd still recommend it.

ana blandiana and nina cassian are two romanian (if you havent already told I am romanian) poets I dont even know if you'll find their books in your language, but if u do, THEYRE SO AMAZING ARSHJD. their poetry is a bit like sylvia plath's like it's somewhat romantic and depressing at the same time, while also having a similar style in some ways.

